6-97%", "Republican nominee Victor Marx has divided his own party and drawn negative coverage", "Colorado's D+6 lean favors Democrats, though no public general-election polls exist"], "rationale": "Colorado's Democratic lean, a Republican nominee whose candidacy has splintered his own party, and unanimous Solid-or-better Democratic ratings from every major forecaster all point to a comfortable Democratic hold of this open seat. Betting markets price Weiser's win chances at 96-97%, and Marx's rapid campaign spending limits his ability to close the gap.", "watch": "A late surge of outside spending for Marx or a major Weiser stumble could tighten the race, since no public polls have directly tested this matchup.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Jared Polis (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Colorado's governorship is open this year as Jared Polis terms out, and Democrats have turned to Attorney General Phil Weiser while Republicans nominated Victor Marx, a candidate whose unusual background and rhetoric have divided his own party. Every major forecaster rates the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and betting markets give Weiser roughly a 96-97% chance of winning.\n\nThe state's Democratic lean of about six points gives Weiser a structural cushion, and his fundraising has kept pace with Marx, whose campaign is burning through its cash quickly. Marx has skipped some debates and drawn negative coverage, while Weiser is already canvassing in Republican-leaning Mesa County. With no public general-election polls available, the picture rests on ratings, markets and fundamentals, all pointing the same direction: a likely comfortable Democratic hold, with the main risk being a late shift in the campaign's final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9695, "margin": 12.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9628, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem